# Weight profile hy4-3.08: Tencent's Hy4-flash in our EXL3 pack at 3.08 bpw (experts at 3 bits, attention, shared
# experts, the head and the Engram tables at 5), converted from the BF16 checkpoint at revision d88c9dfd. 103.1 GB
# on disk with its tables. Switch with ops/use-profile.sh hy4-3.08.
QSE_HY4_BPW=3.08
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Hy4-flash-EXL3-3.0
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=main
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=103.1
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the load took 74.5 GiB at 262,144 tokens, plus the server's prefill workspace
# estimate at that window (7.3) and the 15 GiB floor
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=97
# OPS-308: the engine's limits, as every family's. Ceiling: the load with one lane and the pool off reserves 73.40
# GiB on both packs (hold 1b on aa596e81: 64.02 allocated on 3.08, 72.67 on 3.56; on 3.08 about 9.4 GiB of it sit
# free in the allocator, which no hand-back returned) + 11.6 for the caches and the reserve a request leaves
# = 85; peak: this ceiling + the prefill workspace at 262,144 tokens (7.3) = 92. With the pool the policy takes slot 0's
# window off both (4.12) and adds the side slots' share (3.22 GiB at 8 lanes in hold 1b): 84.10 / 91.10 GiB, over the
# 72.50 GiB the 8-lane load reserves. 85 is the whole number at or under hold 1b's 84.22 / 91.22 on hy4-3.56 (P4 and
# P5 passed there, P5's 64k prompt at 75.12 GiB reserved at most); both packs take the same, as they reserve the same
MEM_CEILING_GIB=85
MEM_PEAK_GIB=92
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_hy4.env"
